<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Cortona</h1><p class="st-meta">1325 CE – 1411 CE · capital Cortona</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Casali family's lordship over the Tuscan hill town of Cortona, which ended when the king of Naples sold it to Florence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cortona">Cortona</a>, an Etruscan hill town above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/val-di-chiana">Valdichiana</a>, had long been a self-governing commune and gained its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> in 1325. That year <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranieri-casali">Ranieri Casali</a>, head of a leading local family, became lord of the city, which the Casali then ruled as a hereditary lordship.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Casali governed a small territory of hill and plain between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-arezzo">Arezzo</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-siena">Siena</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-perugia">Perugia</a>, balancing between these neighbours and seeking imperial and papal recognition. Family murders over the succession were common. Little is known of their administration beyond the town's walls and the fortress they built.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1409 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-of-naples">Ladislaus of Naples</a> captured <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cortona">Cortona</a> from the last Casali lord during his wars in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. In 1411 he sold the town to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-florence">Republic of Florence</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1325 CE – 1411 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.07